{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"refutable-meaningful-borzoi","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Settle the unsettled trust-model decisions the vaquita escalation surfaced, before any code-review-reuse implementation. Decide: (a) the identity notion for reuse (confirm env_id/principal-under-own-key, or switch to key-fingerprint / pinned trusted-environment identity); (b) the NEW code-review op-cert kind slot + its policy entry (only plan-review and completion-verifier exist today); (c) the authenticated diff/ref MATERIAL fingerprint a code-review attestation binds (e.g. {ticket_id, base..head range, diff content hash, merged_log_commit}) — none exists today; (d) how diff-oriented review-code binds to a ticket (via the change's rebar-ticket: trailer?) and composes with the ADR 0088 unsigned session:<id> convergence artifact; (e) whether a REUSED code-review attestation may satisfy the Gerrit LLM-Review +1 merge vote and across which environments (ADR 0013/0020 trust boundary). Output: an accepted ADR. Blocks the code-review producer/consumer story.","id":"987c-67d0-258e-4069","parent_id":"3d86-9fc2-6095-4c69","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR: attestation reuse — identity scope + code-review op-cert kind + merge-vote trust boundary"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787594221879314001,"uuid":"36032cba-17dc-41f2-9d4c-4c4572796355"}